The method `useOrMaybeSuppress` can be simplified by directly updating the `AtomicReference` without creating a new instance every time. This could reduce unnecessary object creation and improve performance slightly.
```java
private void useOrMaybeSuppress(AtomicReference<DeletionExceptions> aex, Exception e) {
    DeletionExceptions current = aex.get();
    if (current.count < MAX_DELETE_EXCEPTIONS) {
        Exception newException = ExceptionsHelper.useOrSuppress(current.exception, e);
        aex.compareAndSet(current, new DeletionExceptions(newException, current.count + 1));
    }
}
